WEBVTT

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.760
Fubuki and the rest of my team
were killed by an animal.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.980
The animals here attack us
because that's how they stay alive.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.350
But you, you're a human!

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.280
FROST DESCENDS

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.950
That's ironic.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.450
Hana ultimately died by drowning.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:07.290
Which means she went out
the same way her mother did.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:08.410
That just goes to show you,

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.170
the sins of the parents
fall upon the children.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.880
Stop it.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.760
Stop being so quick
to pull out weapons all the time.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:28.100
Relying on those things will only
make you forget the value of human life!

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.640
We're not animals,

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:32.980
so why do you insist on
killing fellow humans?

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.360
Precisely because they're human.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.110
Animals don't try to deceive us
or condemn us,

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.490
and they certainly don't laugh
at our pain.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.290
What was Ms. Hana so guilty of?

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.950
What did she ever do to you?

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.210
Are you going to keep blaming her father?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.790
Hana's presence here causes disorder.

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.210
That's a problem.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:59.090
Our team has both the duty
and the right to fix that.

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.890
We're in charge of assuring
that you all live in peace.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.600
Anything disturbing that peace
must be eliminated.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:05.930
Then what about me?

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:06.970
Haru.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.930
Why did you try to kill me?

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.440
For the same reason.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.860
If Ryo hadn't tried to do it himself,
then I would have.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.110
You have no right!

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.980
Nobody has the right to kill others!

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.740
-Nobody!
-Sure we do.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:23.030
We have that right because we survived
absolute hell to get here.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.660
<i>Nobody is watching over us anymore.</i>

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.490
<i>Nobody can judge us anymore.</i>

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.830
Never disobey us again,
or else we'll kill you too!

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:35.290
Back off!

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.550
Koruri.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.010
These two are dangerous.
Keep your distance.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.130
Please tell me, Ango.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.890
I saw you back there.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:46.640
<i>You were right next to Hana.</i>

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:48.350
I need to know!

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.720
Did you push her into that river?

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:52.980
I didn't push her.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:55.730
She backed away from me
and fell in on her own.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.770
But you didn't help her,

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.150
even though you were close by
and had a rope at the ready.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.950
I figured these two
would be able to save her.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:08.370
Even if I had thrown her the rope,
I doubt she would have grabbed on to it.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.330
You abandoned her.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:12.540
You just watched.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.080
First, Ryo cut her rope,
and then you did nothing.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:19.250
You're just like our professors back then.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.340
<i>We couldn't save the others.</i>

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.970
<i>We didn't make it in time.</i>

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.010
<i>There was nothing we could do.</i>

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.430
<i>And the professors just watched it all.</i>

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:32.100
You're the same, Ango!

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:33.730
What you did was exactly the same!

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.230
Why?

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:38.060
You know how horrible it feels!
You experienced it yourself!

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.900
How could you do this, Ango?

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.070
Because I know the consequences.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.780
You just wanted to cover-up your crime.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:52.160
Explain it any way you want,
but you just wanted to hide your crime.

00:04:52.450 --> 00:04:53.660
It makes me sick.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:54.620
Madonna!

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.750
What crime did he commit?

00:04:56.870 --> 00:05:00.800
The truth is,
Ango tried to rape Hana yesterday.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:02.090
Ayu!

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.680
You were ripping off her underwear.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.470
If I hadn't come by when I did,

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.270
I'm sure that you would have
had your way with her.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.640
No... You're wrong.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.770
That's not what I was doing. I was just...

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:22.150
So that's why Ms. Hana told me
to keep all of the women safe.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:26.150
That would also explain
why she asked me to keep Kurumi safe.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.200
You're a fucking scumbag!

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:31.410
No, that's not what...

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.540
Hana has a boyfriend, you know!

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.000
She was always so worried about him.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.500
You're the worst! You asshole!

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:41.420
<i>Is something wrong, Ms. Hana?</i>

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.130
<i>I'm just slacking off.</i>

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.550
<i>Digging that well is a lot of work.</i>

00:05:57.730 --> 00:06:01.730
He is surprisingly strong.
Much more than his looks let on.

00:06:02.270 --> 00:06:04.480
You sheltered kids can't compare.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:09.110
Only a Koshien Tournament star pitcher has
the mettle to survive alone for so long.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.490
I don't think Ms. Hana would ask us
to kill you for what you've done.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:18.160
She knows that would only put her
on the same level as you.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.290
But if this is the true nature of humans,

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.800
then I'd rather be an animal.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.550
Living with them is far better.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:30.840
Let's not get too extreme.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:33.220
We can handle this like reasonable people.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:38.560
Yes, it's clear now that some of
these folks aren't deserving of our pity.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:42.270
Sakuya, are you crying?

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:45.400
To be honest, I really liked Hana.

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.950
But personal feelings shouldn't sway
the outcome of a trial.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:50.280
A trial?

00:06:50.360 --> 00:06:51.570
It's only natural.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.160
Those who commit crimes go to trial.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:56.830
Roughly speaking, there's attempted rape,

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:59.580
assault, coercion, damage to property,

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.670
violation of the Firearms and Swords
Control Law,

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.880
as well as unlawful assembly
with dangerous weapons.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:08.420
And let's not forget
the murder of Mr. Izayoi.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.140
Of course, there are no lawyers or judges,

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.350
and we can't scientifically analyze
the evidence.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.640
That naturally means more weight
will be given to your confession.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.270
Your motive was to prevent disorder.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:21.940
Do you admit your guilt?

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:28.780
We must act swiftly to uphold the law.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:33.240
Well, normally, this would call for
something like imprisonment or exile.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:34.990
What do you all want to do?

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.910
Then our team will just leave.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.290
Let's go, guys.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:43.330
I can't leave Ms. Kurumi behind.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:46.590
Ban, are you kidding?

00:07:46.670 --> 00:07:47.710
Ango.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.880
If Ban is staying,
then I'm doing the same.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:51.840
Gengoro!

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:56.470
There's livestock here for me to care for,
and other things I've left unfinished.

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:58.310
I'm still concerned about those bats too.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:00.020
You must be kidding, Gengoro!

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.020
Let's get out of here!

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:05.310
Ango, I dove into the cold water
that swept away Ms. Hana.

00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:08.230
It was absolutely freezing.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.990
I want to keep learning new things.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:15.910
And I think I can do that by staying here
and being with all these people.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.410
I'm definitely not going with you.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:21.250
You're a huge disappointment.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.460
Koruri!

00:08:27.080 --> 00:08:28.040
Fine!

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.130
You'll all regret this!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:31.760
Let's go, Ryo.

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:35.510
Where have you been, Nijiko?

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.720
Underground, to look at that river.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:40.220
There was an entrance
a lot closer than we thought.

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:45.730
By using a windmill and a water wheel,
I think we can create a supply system.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.360
I'm going to be busy making that happen.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.780
So I can't go either, Ryo.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.940
Nijiko.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.650
Can you help me with this?

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.280
"Help"? I'm going to lead this.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.910
These guys are too damn good.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.790
They've hijacked the group
right out from under us, Ango.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.800
Never show your sorry hides again.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.260
Ango, make sure to ice your hand
and set it in a cast.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:17.430
You don't think they'll come back
for revenge, do you?

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.890
No way,
they've got too much pride for that.

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:22.520
But you know, Ran,

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:24.560
it's okay if you want to cry too.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.560
What?

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.770
You were fond of Hana. I could tell.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.570
How are you holding up, Mr. Aramaki?

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.400
Are you okay with how this turned out?

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:36.110
I'm also...

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:38.160
going to leave.

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:39.950
WATER, HOME

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:42.790
The area between us
and the water source that we found

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.620
looks pretty much like this, right?

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.750
There's a huge difference in elevation.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:50.790
Our first step should be to install
a water wheel to pump the water out.

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:52.500
Really? I'm not sure that's necessary.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:56.470
How exactly do you plan to get it up
the long climb going here, anyway?

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.760
Using a siphon?
That would mean major construction.

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:02.310
We build a windmill at the top
to pull the water up.

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.100
Except the wind hardly blows at all.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:05.680
Then we power it manually.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:09.310
Personally, I think it's more realistic
to make reservoirs midway and pump...

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:16.150
Excuse me.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.160
Please don't jump in
hoping to follow after her.

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:21.410
That's not what I'm here for.

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.080
I figured that it might wash up
on shore somewhere.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:31.500
Then maybe the dogs could sniff it out.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:37.010
So you believe that Hana survived
and washed ashore somewhere downstream?

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:41.220
I think there's a very slim chance.
But, yes.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:45.010
I heard you were going to leave.
Is that so you can find Hana?

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:49.640
Hana left her shoes behind.
The dogs can search for her using those.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:53.610
I'd also like to look for
the other members of Team Spring.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.270
I hope you can find them.

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.780
If Hana really did survive,

00:10:57.860 --> 00:11:00.910
the low water temperature
might be a good thing.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:02.820
Ms. Ayu.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.490
I owe you a debt of gratitude.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.040
You're the one who saved Ms. Hana
when she was assaulted by Ango.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.920
Thank you very much.

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:15.710
I didn't really save her.
I just happened to be passing by.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:19.550
But seeing stuff like that irks me so bad,

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:23.090
I want to beat the crap out of that guy.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.680
I feel the same way.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.560
Men are perfectly capable of
controlling themselves.

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:31.810
Ango just made excuses
to avoid feeling any guilt.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:33.270
He's a coward.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:36.980
I had led myself to believe
Ango wasn't that type of person.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:41.320
I was sure that the chosen few
would all be pure and noble people.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:48.330
The vulgar and foolish people
of the world should all be dead.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:51.710
You seem rather happy about that.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:55.250
Who wouldn't be?

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.090
Why do you all seem to think...

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:02.510
We can use the meat and fat from that one.

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.510
But those claws are sharp.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.430
It's dangerous. Stand back!

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:19.280
I don't understand why
you had bothered to tell me to stand back.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.280
In times like these, anybody who's capable
should step up to the plate.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.290
Oh, I didn't realize
these aquatic plants grew down here.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:33.580
They're delicious
if you dry and grill them.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.210
Do you know a lot about
the plants of this world?

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.210
I wouldn't say "a lot."

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:40.550
Would you mind teaching me?

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.880
I'd like to learn as much as I can.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:49.390
Like I said, this is the only way
we can get the water up here.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.220
Do you plan to do it by hand every day?

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.390
Your plan requires too much work.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.390
It'll be the rainy season
before we finish.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:56.770
They're still at it.

00:12:56.980 --> 00:13:00.980
Yes, neither of them can agree on
the best way to get water.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:02.530
Where'd you get that?

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:04.400
It came to the river for a drink.

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.740
That figures.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.660
All the animals around here
must know where the water is.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:11.740
Oh, hey Ms. Ran?

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:16.920
This may be a silly idea, but instead of
building a system to get the water here,

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.590
what if we just moved closer
to where the water is?

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:24.760
Oh, my apologies.
I didn't mean any disrespect.

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.380
That makes sense.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:30.100
It's feasible,
like a villa just for the dry season.

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:31.510
Works for me.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:38.270
We can't afford to waste water,
so check for leaks.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.480
There's no telling how long it will last.

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:42.400
Let's dig an aqueduct and store some.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.900
Connect that part to this hole
so that it can flow properly.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:46.900
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:48.910
The ground is hard.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:52.910
I've been meaning to ask, Nijiko.
Why did you stay?

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.330
You seemed real friendly with Ryo.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:59.120
Without me, this group would have
no one left who took the water class.

00:13:59.710 --> 00:14:01.880
I thought it best
to keep my priorities straight.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:03.800
We would have managed.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.380
Are you that hung up on your duty?

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:08.880
It's more than that.
It was imprinted on me from a young age.

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:12.760
In any case,
I'm taking charge of building the house.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.640
Then don't interfere with
the water system.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.480
Those two are getting along well.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:20.730
Get back to work, Akiwo.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:21.690
Okay.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.110
<i>Even though you're gone,
life continues like normal.</i>

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.530
<i>Are you really dead, Hana?</i>

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.530
<i>After all that crazy stuff
we survived together.</i>

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.250
<i>You were always so stubborn
and pushy about everything.</i>

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.420
<i>But then you vanished
in the blink of an eye.</i>

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:44.420
<i>When I really think about it,</i>

00:14:45.130 --> 00:14:47.970
<i>I haven't even known you for very long.</i>

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:52.640
<i>But to me, it felt like a lifetime.</i>

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.220
Are you okay, Haru?

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:57.890
I'm fine.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.730
It's dangerous to use sharp tools
when you're not focused.

00:15:06.070 --> 00:15:10.740
Koruri, I really hope
you won't regret staying with us.

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:13.700
I won't.
It's not a decision I made lightly.

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.280
But I have to admit,

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:19.000
I'm a little surprised at myself
for not going with Ango.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.830
It's started to slow down. Let's catch it.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:25.790
I'll head to the right.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.100
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:36.100
Ouch.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:38.520
My other fingers feel numb.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:41.520
Shit!
That bastard didn't look like a threat.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.150
I never thought he could throw like that.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:46.270
Could you do that?

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.400
No way.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:50.530
Never underestimate anyone,
no matter how weak they look.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.110
Don't move your hand. Put it in a sling.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.290
It gets pretty cold at night, right?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.420
Ryo, tell me why exactly
you tried to kill Hana.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:07.250
I never actually wanted to kill her.

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.000
Same for Haru.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:12.090
I was surprised when I saw you
knock him down in the swamp.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:15.970
So you just wanted to rape her?

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.930
No, that's not it.
I just wanted to hurt her.

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:23.190
I was angry and the heat had gotten to me.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:24.520
Look, man,

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:26.810
if Hana ended up giving birth,

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:28.770
you would have been too disgusted
to look at it.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:31.740
Do you want Professor Takashi
to have a grandkid?

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.070
Get a grip!

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:36.820
Just admit it.
You didn't think any of this through.

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:39.700
Now you've turned all the women
against us.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.710
Use your brain.
I know you're not an idiot.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:49.840
That's why I knew it would be best
if Hana was taken out of the picture.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:55.340
I'm going to take a look around.
Go sleep in the tent.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.510
And don't move your hand.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:01.850
Remind me, were you always
this thoughtful and caring?

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:05.730
I don't mind
that you're a sorry mess sometimes.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:10.020
But if you keep doing stupid shit,
I might just abandon you.

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:16.110
<i>What am I going to do if it never heals?</i>

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:19.740
<i>I can't survive in this world
without my right hand.</i>

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:24.460
<i>I don't get it.
What the hell is wrong with me?</i>

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.120
<i>Gengoro gave me such a cold look.</i>

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:30.960
<i>Koruri, Ayu, and even Ban.</i>

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.590
<i>I was the one who got injured,
so why are the others more important?</i>

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.590
<i>Nijiko, why would you abandon Ryo?</i>

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.390
<i>Guys, what the hell should I do?</i>

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:44.430
<i>Please tell me.</i>

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:45.890
<i>Shigeru!</i>

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.780
Those two are really
hanging out together a lot lately.

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:56.490
Seems like they're always talking
about plants and trees.

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:59.240
Mr. Aramaki is a sucker for a pretty face.

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:00.870
<i>And so am I.</i>

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:03.870
Haru.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:06.660
What?

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:10.130
Once the dry season house is built,
I'm going to leave.

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.040
But, Mr. Aramaki...

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.340
You're going to stay, right?

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:18.050
You should definitely stay here
with Ms. Koruri.

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:20.140
Please look after Momota as well.

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:23.850
I'll stop by once in a while
to report on my progress.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:27.140
If I come across Ms. Fujiko or the others,
I'll bring them back with me.

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:28.310
Okay.

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:30.350
I'm sorry.

00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:32.770
If Hana was still here,
I would totally go with you.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.440
I know.

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.530
There's a lot that you can do here.
I'm sure of it.

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:42.280
Do your best, Haru.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:46.290
<i>I'm going to look for Ms. Hana
and the rest of Team Spring as well.</i>

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:49.750
<i>But that's not the only reason
I'm leaving.</i>

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:52.290
<i>I hurt Ango badly.</i>

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:57.630
<i>I have violent tendencies within myself,
just like they do.</i>

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:02.590
<i>My right arm was never supposed to be
used for anything like that.</i>

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:06.100
<i>I can't just leave things like this.
I have to change.</i>

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:08.980
Thank you, Haru.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:09.890
What?

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:14.940
<i>I have to continue
to strengthen myself more,</i>

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:18.110
<i>until I'm able to control
every fiber of my being.</i>

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:21.910
<i>Then I can put my power to use
in the right way.</i>

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.740
<i>To save others</i>

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:25.910
<i>and keep them safe as long as I can.</i>

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:27.700
Hey, Taka.

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.120
Do you mind if I come with you?

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:30.910
-What?
-"Taka"?

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.330
Well...

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:35.170
I don't mind,
but it would only be the two of us.

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:37.170
You're a trustworthy guy, right?

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.510
Certainly, but...

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:42.340
I want to explore this world
and examine all the plants within it.

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:44.890
We can collect medicinal herbs
while we're at it.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:52.390
<i>Not long after that</i>

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:55.900
<i>the house for the dry season
was completed and we all moved in.</i>

00:19:57.730 --> 00:20:02.150
<i>Then Mr. Aramaki and Ayu departed
on their journey together.</i>

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.120
Stay safe out there!

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:08.330
Don't forget you're welcome back any time.

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:11.160
Come back to see the baby when it's born.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:17.670
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:22.670
<i>Not only did Ango and Ryo leave,
but now Ayu is going off with Aramaki.</i>

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:26.220
<i>I never imagined that Summer A
would fall apart so easily.</i>

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:32.560
<i>Koruri, you've learned to smile.</i>

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:35.060
<i>Keep reading the wind and clouds.</i>

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:39.730
<i>Gengoro, keep a close eye on the animals
of this world. Study them.</i>

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:43.990
<i>Ban, keep that pregnant girl healthy.
Don't let her die.</i>

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:49.160
<i>Nijiko, why didn't you go with Ryo?</i>

00:20:53.660 --> 00:20:56.790
<i>What are you doing, Ango?
What's wrong with you?</i>

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.260
<i>Big Bro Takashi,
I may have screwed this up.</i>

00:21:06.220 --> 00:21:09.760
Kaname, you're planning to go
to the future with Team B, aren't you?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:12.810
Is that to keep an eye on Team A?

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:15.060
<i>That's part of it.</i>

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:18.900
<i>But more than that, I knew there was
a chance they would fail,</i>

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:21.190
<i>which means I would need to
get rid of them.</i>

00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:24.700
<i>If they killed the guides,
or did anything to harm Hana,</i>

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:29.660
<i>or if they proved to be a hindrance
in this world, I couldn't let them stay.</i>

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:32.120
<i>You're my responsibility, Ango.</i>

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.870
<i>That's why there is a reaper.</i>

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:38.500
What's wrong?

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:39.750
It's weird.

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.550
I feel a presence occasionally.
A bad vibe.

00:21:42.800 --> 00:21:43.760
Really?

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:47.590
Your ability to sense danger is
as dull as a spoon right now.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:52.510
Maybe there's a carnivorous predator
out there.

00:21:53.520 --> 00:21:55.270
<i>Ryo is as sharp as ever.</i>

00:21:55.850 --> 00:21:57.640
<i>I guess I'll keep watching for now.</i>

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:01.770
<i>But I can't figure out
why Ryo is sticking with Ango.</i>

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.200
<i>Somebody...</i>

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:11.740
<i>please tell me.</i>

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:14.200
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:16.710
<i>What am I supposed to do now?</i>

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:22.590
Koruri?

00:22:22.790 --> 00:22:24.050
No, it's not.

00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:25.630
A kite?

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:29.590
Hey, that's a ship.
